The maximum value for DeepSeek and Qwen models is 8192.', example='500'),
      model?: string(name='Model', description='The model name.
Supported models under the aliyun provider:
["qwen-plus", "deepseek-r1", "qwen-omni-turbo"]', example='qwen-plus'),
      params?: map[string]any(name='Params', description='The custom user parameters in key-value pairs. This parameter is deprecated. Use the BizParams parameter instead.', example='{\\"verification_code\\": \\"xxx\\"}'),
      prompt?: string(name='Prompt', description='The prompt used to instruct the model on the role or behavior to adopt.', example='xxxx'),
      temperature?: double(name='Temperature', description='The sampling temperature used to control the randomness and creativity of the generated text. A higher value indicates higher randomness.
Default value: 0.7.
Valid values: 0 to 2, excluding 2.
Note: This parameter does not take effect for deepseek-r1.', example='0.7'),
      toolExecutionConfig?: any(name='ToolExecutionConfig'),
      tools?: [ any ](name='Tools'),
      topP?: double(name='TopP', description='The sampling range used to control the diversity of output tokens. The model samples from tokens whose cumulative probability exceeds this value to ensure the sampling range is not too broad. A higher value indicates a richer variety of output tokens.
